{"title":"2020 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Coordinate_Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Power_of_a_Point_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Power of a Point Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Vertical_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Vertical Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathionaire_(Clear_and_fast_explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathionaire (Clear and fast explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀_Quick_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀 Quick 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a semicircle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af92a37effb62a6c7368d1f2fc5ffd9e1674685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FE},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> as shown in the figure. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/7518b5f1128de37e4c7fe5c006c28cc40de96943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=16,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b178cb0d42a2530a685f5e7bf50425d9d6e3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD=AE=9.$\" width=\"119\" height=\"13\" /> What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d64633b1612a0801fc7f0316fdbdf0adf1f2d70d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD?$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9c1a2a36307aa14183c77012405d57721363d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(arc((0,0),17,180,0)); draw((-17,0)--(17,0)); fill((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle, 1.5*grey); draw((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,(8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,(-8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,(17,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,(-17,0), 1.25*S); label(&quot;$16$&quot;,(0,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(12.5,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-12.5,0),N);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fca3ac8d18bcfd74d7ba1b668fbc1a1ee4fbed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }240 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }248 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }256 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }264 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }272$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/5702f644dac21548c80e93c4d527cd0bec4d0ebb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(arc((0,0),17,180,0)); draw((-17,0)--(17,0)); fill((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle, 1.5*grey); draw((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,(8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,(-8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,(17,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,(-17,0), 1.25*S); label(&quot;$16$&quot;,(0,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(12.5,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-12.5,0),N); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), 1.25*S); draw((0,0)--(-8,15));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the semicircle. The diameter of the semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3dd7d5d33f36d6fec1e291fe9da6b3d7e1844ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+16+9=34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/3843d1289253f18a93c7423bdd0c5d3d15247492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. By symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/c/d7c5e63e3e344d102e5316d0e2b2aba4e2d588a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD=OA=\\frac{16}{2}= 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"161\" height=\"37\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem in right-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1432798ecb03529aff50881ed85d74fedc320e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ODC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0eaa4e3e68ed1f7e987e0d18b6478e7288074980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OBA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />), we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a9202259f727b1e49810a11197d5b5454f1b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{17^2-8^2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. Accordingly, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb2df8a71fe1b2db1c04e5a922288ea62aac641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\cdot 15=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"148\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Coordinate_Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Coordinate_Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Coordinate Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> be the origin. Evidently, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccdb71d6da463d2a5aac80cc95c40998e66f926c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(-8,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2cb0b6b02b2047bcf7380d094d5ce648e686c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(8,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. Since points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> share <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinates with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, it suffices to find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> (which will be the height of the rectangle) and multiply this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> (which we know is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />). The radius of the semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e8f1a8acce50b8b7471df1a11ef49608810bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9+16+9}{2} = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />, so the whole circle has equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c6d941cb90a3858fe63f5e734e2ef37199c034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />; as already stated, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has the same <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so substituting this into the equation shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9c6b66f91de04fcc8572a31122f2bff6ed3c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\pm15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf32406671fc9a01b1982019404e3f981a0f56b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, the y-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7ed9c2a2b447f97646a33ea48f251b915386501a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\cdot 15 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"148\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>(Note that the synthetic solution (Solution 1) is definitely faster and more elegant. However, this is the solution that you should use if you can't see any other easier strategy.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use a result from the Art of Problem Solving <i>Introduction to Algebra</i> book Sidenote: for a semicircle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c2fcaad890e239dd2170317ab995b2329290f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />, such that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> part is on one side and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> part is on the other side, the height from the end of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> side (or the start of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> side) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b58afccd87d49e39a6e850d3121001b0266ae52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />. To use this formula, we scale the figure down by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; this will give the height a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e130f21a4ecd8a7e4726e20e99d11c76cecdfbf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{16+9}{9}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{9}} = \\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"171\" height=\"43\" />. Now, scaling back up by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe18245f20eabd47675dbdeae537f0f71ad395c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot \\frac{5}{3} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />. The answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a9f8984d9589e0b9c26ee26f0e7aefe8d36666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"148\" height=\"28\" />.\n-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Sweetmango77\" title=\"User:Sweetmango77\">SweetMango77</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Power_of_a_Point_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Power_of_a_Point_Theorem)\">Solution 4 (Power of a Point Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Power of a Point Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw the other half of the circle as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfefedd8baaef2f91395070ae886d68688126012.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(arc((0,0),17,360,0)); draw((-17,0)--(17,0)); fill((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle, 1.5*grey); draw((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,(8,0), 1.25*SE); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,(-8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-8,0), 1.25*SW); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,(17,0), 1.25*E); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,(-17,0), 1.25*W); label(&quot;$16$&quot;,(0,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(12.5,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-12.5,0),N); draw((-8,-15)--(-8,0)--(8,0)--(8,-15)--cycle); dot(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;,(8,-15), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;,(-8,-15), 1.25*S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"225\" />\nBy the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point_Theorem\" title=\"Power of a Point Theorem\">Power of a Point Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f642dc46bf73cba517e037b666ed4f8b683aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD\\cdot DE = CD\\cdot C&#39;D$\" width=\"174\" height=\"14\" />. By symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30bafdee48986fe35d47cd17d9741ff7c3132999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = C&#39;D$\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed029412e5d6211091c99437abc55958528085f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = 9$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e713fdb3aefa496facabfeb671a526ad7f627841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 16 + 9 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting in these values, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d5934976888f1a59a9dedf14390d9a5e94baef46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot 25 = CD^2$\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d18ed8278105caf6ac638da8dca07f34a112ac48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD^2 = 225$\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbad9873141337a76316839309a015fa3b67010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe area of the rectangle is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d702f9149dcc6a5b75c827682add5650dee0adf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\cdot 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"148\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Vertical_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Vertical_Theorem)\">Solution 5 (Vertical Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Vertical Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5986c8ddd9913ea22a77d81d176ce8b3b5ac5bcc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw(arc((0,0),17,180,0)); draw((-17,0)--(17,0)); fill((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle, 1.5*grey); draw((-8,0)--(-8,15)--(8,15)--(8,0)--cycle); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,(8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,(-8,15), 1.25*N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-8,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,(17,0), 1.25*S); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,(-17,0), 1.25*S); label(&quot;$16$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(12.5,0),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(-12.5,0),N); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, (0,15), SE); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), NE); draw((0,0)--(0, 15)); draw((-7.5,15)--(0,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p>According to the Pythagorean Theorem and the Vertical Theorem, we can find out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19c72674377e06fd0edca7d0cb251518857a2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OG=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{2\\times9+16}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{16}{2}\\right)^2}=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"311\" height=\"56\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f85555156449803515a001cc2ec66176cbce49a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\times16=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"30\" />;\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Bloggish\" title=\"User:Bloggish\">Bloggish</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=_0fveg1r3WFmwmpw&amp;t=3334\">https://youtu.be/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=_0fveg1r3WFmwmpw&amp;t=3334</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathionaire_.28Clear_and_fast_explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathionaire_(Clear_and_fast_explanation)\">Video Solution by Mathionaire (Clear and fast explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathionaire (Clear and fast explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P1xjpqm9_DQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P1xjpqm9_DQ</a>\n</p><p>~Mathionaire\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_.28Easy_to_understand.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHNrBwwUCMI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bHNrBwwUCMI</a>\n</p><p>~NiuniuMaths\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_Quick_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀_Quick_🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀 Quick 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀 Quick 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pA6Smw91Bc0\">https://youtu.be/pA6Smw91Bc0</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go\">Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Qo4pG3Uk_U\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Qo4pG3Uk_U</a>\n</p><p>~North America Math Contest Go Go Go\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/l9wZS3qGSCg\">https://youtu.be/l9wZS3qGSCg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VnOecUiP-SA\">https://youtu.be/VnOecUiP-SA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YnwkBZTv5Fw?t=852\">https://youtu.be/YnwkBZTv5Fw?t=852</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7SwJdAEOeAg?t=23\">https://youtu.be/7SwJdAEOeAg?t=23</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S_CnKCuOA_w\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S_CnKCuOA_w</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mGQw1yALXYM&amp;t=2524s\">https://youtu.be/mGQw1yALXYM&amp;t=2524s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8\" title=\"2020 AMC 8\">2020 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br